ary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Archive</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/submit/\">Submissions</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/apod-index/\">Index</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/apod-search/\">Search</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/apod-calendar/\">Calendar</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/feed/apod-basic/\">RSS</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/apod-education/\">Education</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/apod-about/\">About</a></li><li class=\"usa-nav__primary-item \"><a class=\"usa-nav__link\" href=\"https://asterisk.apod.com/discuss_apod.php?date=040501\" rel=\"noopener\">Discuss</a></li></ul></nav></div><div class=\"hds-secondary-navigation-menu-spacer\">&nbsp;</div></div></div></div></div>\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-media-detail-hero nasa-gb-align-wide width-full maxw-full margin-y-5 desktop:margin-y-7 padding-x-3 media-detail-hero--suppress-inner-media-caption hds-module alignwide wp-block-nasa-blocks-media-detail-hero\">\t<div class=\"grid-container grid-container-block padding-x-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"label margin-bottom-1\">APOD</p>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"heading-22 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-2\">Astronomy Picture of the Day</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3 media-detail-hero__subtext\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer.\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"media-detail-hero__media margin-bottom-6\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"wp-block-smd-block-image-rollover smd-image-rollover hds-module hds-media smd-image-rollover--clickable-indicators\"><div class=\"smd-image-rollover__alignment margin-left-auto margin-right-auto nasa-block-align-full\"><div class=\"smd-image-rollover__frame\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"462\" height=\"598\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_f2.jpg?w=462&amp;h=598&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"smd-image-rollover__image smd-image-rollover__image--primary\" alt=\"See Explanation. Moving the cursor over the image will bring up an annotated version. Clicking on the image will bring up the highest resolution version available.\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_f2.jpg?w=462&amp;h=598&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 462w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_f2.jpg?w=232&amp;h=300&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 232w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_f2.jpg?w=309&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 309w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 462px) 100vw, 462px\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"462\" height=\"598\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_c2.jpg?w=462&amp;h=598&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"smd-image-rollover__image smd-image-rollover__image--secondary\" alt=\"See Explanation. Moving the cursor over the image will bring up an annotated version. Clicking on the image will bring up the highest resolution version available.\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_c2.jpg?w=462&amp;h=598&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 462w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_c2.jpg?w=232&amp;h=300&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 232w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/cds/apod/apod/2004/may/mvms_042304_richard_c2.jpg?w=309&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 309w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 462px) 100vw, 462px\" /><div class=\"toggle-button-container padding-1\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"toggle-view-before-button margin-right-1px is-active\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><span class=\"toggle-view-before-label\">Image 1</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"toggle-view-after-button margin-left-1px\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><span class=\"toggle-view-after-label\">Image 2</span></button></div></div></div></div>\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h1 class=\"display-48 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3\">A Western Sky at Twilight</h1>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row media-detail-hero__content-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-0 media-detail-hero__description\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Explanation:</strong> On April 23rd, the Moon along with planets Saturn, Mars, and Venus (and planet Earth of course &#8230;) <a href=\"http://science.nasa.gov/headlines/y2004/ 21apr_planets2.htm\" target=\"_blank\">were all visible</a> in the west at twilight, captured here from a site near Saylorvillle Lake north of Des Moines, Iowa, USA. Putting <a href=\"http://www.fourmilab.ch/yoursky/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">your cursor</a> over the image will label our fellow solar system wanderers and also reveal the approximate trajectory of the <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap001014.html\" rel=\"noopener\">ecliptic plane</a> &#8211; defined by Earth&#8217;s orbit around the Sun &#8211; angling above the western horizon. After sunset tonight, the western sky will present a similar arrangement of planets, although the Moon will have moved east out of the picture, passing bright Jupiter along the ecliptic and heading for <a href=\"http://www.xs4all.nl/~carlkop/eclipsmaan/leclips2004.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">May 4th&#8217;s total lunar eclipse</a> . May <a href=\"http://skyandtelescope.com/observing/objects/comets/ article_1238_1.asp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">could also</a> be a good month <a href=\"http://skyandtelescope.com/observing/objects/comets/ article_1229_2.asp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">for comets</a> .\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"display-none desktop:display-block desktop:grid-col-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-5 margin-top-3 desktop:margin-top-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<table class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-table width-full\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tbody>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Date</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tMay 1, 2004\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Credit</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t Credit &amp; Copyright:  Stan Richard\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Authors &amp; editors:</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.mtu.edu/physics/department/faculty/nemiroff/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Robert Nemiroff</a> (<a href=\"https://www.mtu.edu/physics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MTU</a>) &amp; <a href=\"https://inspirehep.net/authors/1073087\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jerry Bonnell</a> (<a href=\"https://www.astro.umd.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UMCP</a>)\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">A service of:</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://science.gsfc.nasa.gov/astrophysics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ASD</a> at <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NASA</a> / <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/centers/goddard/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GSFC</a>,<br /><a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/learn/about-science-activation/\" target=\"_blank\">NASA Science Activation</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://www.mtu.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Michigan Tech. U.</a>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tbody>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</table>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"nasa-gb-align-wide nasa-button-link padding-y-1 padding-x-0 hds-module alignwide wp-block-nasa-blocks-related-link\">\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/random-apod/\" target=\"_self\" class=\"button-primary button-primary-md link-external-false\" aria-label=\"Random APOD Generator\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"line-height-alt-1\">Random APOD Generator</span>\n\t\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 32 32\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><circle class=\"button-primary-circle\" cx=\"16\" cy=\"16\" r=\"16\"></circle><path d=\"M8 16.956h12.604l-3.844 4.106 1.252 1.338L24 16l-5.988-6.4-1.252 1.338 3.844 4.106H8v1.912z\" class=\"color-spacesuit-white\"></path></svg>\n\t\t</a>\n\t\n\t</div>\n\n\n<div style=\"height:1px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-module alignwide wp-block-smd-block-next-prev\">            <div class=\"smd-next-prev-buttons-titles\">\n            <a class=\"smd-next-prev__prev\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2004-april-30-eyeful-of-saturn/\">\n                <div class=\"hds-next-prev-nav-arrow hds-next-prev-arrow-prev\">\n                    <svg version=\"1.1\" x=\"0px\" y=\"0px\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\"><path class=\"st0\" d=\"M3.5,4.5l3.7-3.6L6.3,0L1.8,4.5L6.3,9l0.9-0.9L3.5,4.5z\"></path></svg>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"smd-next-prev-buttons-titles__content\">\n                    <div class=\"smd-next-prev-buttons-titles__prev-label\">\n                        Yesterday&#039;s Image                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"smd-next-prev-buttons-titles__prev\">\n                        APOD: 2004 April 30 &#8211; Eyeful of Saturn                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </a>\n            <a class=\"smd-next-prev__next\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2004-may-2-io-in-true-color/\">\n                <div class=\"smd-next-prev-buttons-titles__content\">\n                    <div class=\"smd-next-prev-buttons-titles__next-label\">\n                        Tomorrow&#039;s Image                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"smd-next-prev-buttons-titles__next\">\n                        APOD: 2004 May 2 &#8211; Io in True Color                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"hds-next-prev-nav-arrow hds-next-prev-arrow-next\">\n                    <svg version=\"1.1\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x=\"0px\" y=\"0px\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\"><path class=\"st0\" d=\"M5.5,4.5L1.8,8.1L2.7,9l4.5-4.5L2.7,0L1.8,0.9L5.5,4.5z\"></path></svg>\n